WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:07.510
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week
Doctor Who was a big Clara story with a very

00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:08.720
big WTF reveal.

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:12.520
So I feel like that’s what we should spend
most of our time talking about.

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:17.430
There were a lot of great gags and some good
social commentary, so let’s start with Top

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:19.849
5 moments and then I’ll do my review.

00:00:19.849 --> 00:00:25.470
New Giveaway starts now, all you have to do
to enter is be a subscriber and leave a comment.

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:28.269
Careful for spoilers, here we go.

00:00:28.269 --> 00:00:29.989
Top 5 Moments

00:00:29.989 --> 00:00:31.339
Number 5 - The Tiny TARDIS

00:00:31.339 --> 00:00:36.629
Great gag that provides the reason for Clara
turning into Doctor Clara.

00:00:36.629 --> 00:00:40.020
The Doctor is freaking out and people are
vanishing so there is a sense of urgency.

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:45.010
But I feel like the locked room mystery storyline
makes them completely forget the tension between

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:46.010
them.

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:49.519
Last week during Mummy they said weeks had
passed, so it seems like by the time things

00:00:49.519 --> 00:00:55.660
really get going, Clara has completely done
a 180 on hating the Doctor and is ignoring

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:56.989
Danny’s phone calls.

00:00:56.989 --> 00:01:03.379
I think a couple of my favorite Tiny TARDIS
gags were the walking hand from Addams family

00:01:03.379 --> 00:01:11.230
on the Train Tracks, any time he passed Clara
something normal size, like it was one of

00:01:11.230 --> 00:01:14.790
the handbags from the Jetsons Cartoon.

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:15.870
And Siege Mode.

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:19.840
The TARDIS in siege mode looked a lot like
the Pandorica.

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:24.270
And to be fair, he said that while it was
locked down, nobody could get in or out.

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:28.460
Which was the whole point of the pandorica,
to contain The Doctor.

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:30.430
I don’t think there’s any special significance
to it.

00:01:30.430 --> 00:01:34.450
They just wanted it to look like a super strong
indestructible cube.

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:38.330
The Door of the TARDIS was also a nice nod
to the shrinking door in Charlie and The Chocolate

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:42.290
Factory, the classic Gene Wilder movie, actually
I think that was called Willy Wonka and the

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:46.070
Chocolate Factory.

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:55.080
Number 4 - Two Dimensional Languages

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:58.610
Math is always going to be the Universal Language,
so that wasn’t a huge surprise.

00:01:58.610 --> 00:02:02.250
In real life, when nations send transmissions
into deep space, they always broadcast mathematical

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:03.250
formulas.

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:04.250
The Doctor used Pi.

00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:15.740
It was a fun bit of science that turned into
a great gag.

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:24.750
I always love the stories he slips in when
he’s solving similar problems.

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:28.750
Like the Gas Creatures that communicate with
belches of flame and the stomach creatures

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:29.750
that say hello by digesting.

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:31.239
Douglas Mackinnon wrote the episode, so at
some point he sat down and had to think of

00:02:31.239 --> 00:02:32.239
crazy sounding aliens and think of weird non-human
ways for them to speak.

00:02:32.239 --> 00:02:33.239
That’s one of my favorite things about science
fiction.

00:02:33.239 --> 00:02:35.470
Just working through the mechanics of simple
things like that.

00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:37.770
In the end the aliens seemed more like an
invasion force than an exploration team.

00:02:37.770 --> 00:02:41.080
But it did make you wonder if The Doctor would
find a way to use the TARDIS to enter the

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:42.200
second dimension.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:59.850
Physics was a big thing in the episode, so
there were a lot of TARDIS facts being thrown

00:02:59.850 --> 00:03:01.030
around.

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:04.530
Like flattening the surface of the earth.

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:06.620
That’s actually true by the way.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:11.040
The TARDIS is powered by the eye of harmony,
which is like a dying star.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:16.670
The mass of that just by itself is so great
it’s ridiculous.

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:19.690
Number 3 - Everybody Is Turning Into Banksy
Paintings

00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:28.849
The Graffiti People aspect provided some nice
social commentary.

00:03:28.849 --> 00:03:32.210
The creatures were transporting people into
the second dimension and dissecting them for

00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:33.210
study.

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:34.210
That’s what the wall art was all about.

00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:37.660
Eventually they learn to use the bodies to
exist in three dimensional space.

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:43.980
They fudge the logic a little bit on that
part, but I usually give Doctor Who a pass

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:45.230
when it comes to science.

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:49.480
It’s meant to be fiction, so when it gets
a little ridiculous it doesn’t take me out

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:50.710
of the story too much.

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:53.330
I did really like The Doctor’s 2 Dimensional
Gun that clara used to transform things.

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:56.260
It reminded me of David Tennant’s machine
that goes Ding.

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:59.680
The Graffiti artist was played by Joivan Wade.

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:02.730
He was great as far as pudding brains go.

00:04:02.730 --> 00:04:05.210
I love how quickly the Doctor turns around
on people.

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:06.500
No wait, he might be useful.

00:04:06.500 --> 00:04:07.880
Don’t scare him off.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:11.800
Number 2 - Doctor Oswald

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:13.420
So many things we could say about this.

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:17.400
One, it’s probably the closest we’ll get
to seeing a female Doctor in the short term.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:20.820
Not accounting for the fact Missy might be
a Time Lady.

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:24.309
But a Time Lady isn’t the same thing as
a Lady Doctor.

00:04:24.309 --> 00:04:27.279
Either way, it was a big moment in Doctor
Who history.

00:04:27.279 --> 00:04:31.550
I love that later in the episode the Doctor
turns his congratulations into something darker.

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:34.979
When he was getting ready to die he sounded
really happy about her playacting as him,

00:04:34.979 --> 00:04:38.379
but at the end of the episode he made me think
he knows something is going on a la Missy.

00:04:38.379 --> 00:04:41.159
I don’t think he knows about Missy, I just
think he knows something isn’t right with

00:04:41.159 --> 00:04:42.159
Clara.

00:04:42.159 --> 00:04:45.980
I’ve seen a lot of blog posts recently about
the show presenting Clara as if she were a

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:48.389
Time Lady, technically she’s the impossible
girl.

00:04:48.389 --> 00:04:54.340
But since she’s been a companion, the stories
have given her so much authority the Doctor

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:56.050
rolls over for her all the time.

00:04:56.050 --> 00:05:09.539
He even called her Boss.

00:05:09.539 --> 00:05:15.809
Now that we know Missy has something to do
with Clara, it makes you wonder if Moffat

00:05:15.809 --> 00:05:17.639
is trying to say something about her true
nature.

00:05:17.639 --> 00:05:23.050
I think my favorite Doctor Clara moments were
Jenna Coleman doing a version of the Matt

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:34.360
Smith Doctor when he would get all crazy with
an idea.

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:38.509
Like when she thought to trick the two dimensional
beings into recharging the TARDIS and of course

00:05:38.509 --> 00:05:41.219
when she said “I am The Doctor”

00:05:41.219 --> 00:05:44.710
Very good lying Doctor Oswald.

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:49.309
Until the big twist at the end it felt like
this episode was all about The Doctor teaching

00:05:49.309 --> 00:05:51.880
Clara how to be The Doctor.

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:55.919
and my Number 1 WTF Moment - Missy is connected
to Clara

00:05:55.919 --> 00:05:57.370
In case you were confused.

00:05:57.370 --> 00:06:01.990
Missy was watching Clara in the same way The
Doctor was watching Clara on the TARDIS console.

00:06:01.990 --> 00:06:07.750
Not exactly the same way.

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:11.370
I saw some of you on twitter thought that
Missy was looking through Clara’s eyes like

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:14.050
she was jacked into Clara the same way The
Doctor was.

00:06:14.050 --> 00:06:18.560
But she was seeing her in third person, so
either that scene on her ipad there was from

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:23.960
a few minutes ago when The Doctor was talking
to her and Missy is jacked into him or she’s

00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:26.909
watching Clara in some other way.

00:06:26.909 --> 00:06:30.469
This is what we should spend all our time
in the comments talking about.

00:06:30.469 --> 00:06:38.080
Is Missy jacked into The Doctor instead of
Clara or is she just connected to Clara.

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:42.050
I think when we’re seeing Clara on this
screen the Doctor has already gone back inside

00:06:42.050 --> 00:06:46.419
the TARDIS, so I don’t think she’s jacked
into him.

00:06:46.419 --> 00:07:12.810
But what about the room she’s in, doesn’t
that look kind of like a version of the Doctor’s

00:07:12.810 --> 00:07:14.550
TARDIS with the window holes?

00:07:14.550 --> 00:07:21.469
It seems like more evidence that Missy is
a Time Lady or a dark aspect of the doctor.

00:07:21.469 --> 00:07:25.719
In the past, when the TARDIS has gotten hijacked,
the lights always change color or go down.

00:07:25.719 --> 00:07:29.499
They could just be messing with us a little,
I really want Missy to be a separate person

00:07:29.499 --> 00:07:30.499
from The Doctor.

00:07:30.499 --> 00:07:32.470
It would make it easier for her to come back
at some point.

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:38.069
If it turned out she’s just a dark part
of the doctor’s own mind, she’s really

00:07:38.069 --> 00:07:39.680
just his subconscious acting out.

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:44.150
I just think that would be a big middle finger.

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:49.599
Moffat just saying, it was all in his head
the whole time.

00:07:49.599 --> 00:07:53.650
He does talk to himself a lot, but I still
want Missy to be a separate person.

00:07:53.650 --> 00:07:55.869
It does seem like they’re implying she has
her own TARDIS though.

00:07:55.869 --> 00:07:59.939
So it’s time to Rani Time Lady theorycraft.

00:07:59.939 --> 00:08:05.599
Let me know what your favorite moment in the
episode was and do you think Missy is another

00:08:05.599 --> 00:09:33.149
Time Lady 

00:09:33.149 --> 00:10:11.990
and do you 

00:10:11.990 --> 00:10:14.619
think she’s using Clara?

